obal state/GNS, corner trace/fullness, or the Overleaf theorem -> fix: retain these as explicit open obligations. [Task 2]\n262-\n263:# Task Group: lean/stabilizer standalone Lean tensor-product and trace formalization\n264-\n265-scope: separate, approval-gated Lean audit/formalization of the proposed stabilizer-region tensor-product theorem, including checked algebraic transport and an explicit analytic-theorem stop boundary\n266:applies_to: cwd=lean/stabilizer (source context=source-workspace); reuse_rule=reuse the checked algebraic modules and analytic-obligation checklist only after rechecking pinned mathlib and source assumptions\n267-\n268-## Task 1: audit the manuscript target and formalize the algebraic layer\n--\n270-### rollout_summary_files\n271-\n272:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-02T19-10-40-cRYC-standalone_lean_stabilizer_hyperfinite_formalization_blocked.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/02/rollout-2026-08-02T21-10-40-019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T03:04:54+00:00, thread_id=019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2, partial: algebraic results checked; full theorem blocked)\n273-\n274-### keywords\n--\n280-### rollout_summary_files\n281-\n282:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-02T19-10-40-cRYC-standalone_lean_stabilizer_hyperfinite_formalization_blocked.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/02/rollout-2026-08-02T21-10-40-019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T03:04:54+00:00, thread_id=019fc3e2-abbe-71f2-9c08-db9f0ba1e6f2, blocked: source and library lack required analytic inputs)\n283-\n284-### keywords\n\n--- PLAN P50 ---\n5-The project now has two parallel mathematical targets sharing finite\n6-stabilizer and operator-algebra infrastructure, but neither is allowed to\n7-silently supply the other one's hypotheses.\n8-\n9:### Lane G — general lattices and central type-III exclusion\n10-\n11-**Source basis:** `main.tex:332-342`, with the corner proof at\n12-`main.tex:1026-1536`.\n13-\n--\n42-\n43-### Reconnection\n44-\n45-Lane H gives an explicit factor theorem and, in the infinite-pure case, the\n46:concrete faithful normal semifinite weight `Tr barTensor tau`. Lane G gives\n47-the general no-central-type-III theorem. A final comparison theorem may show\n48-that the Lane-H factor model satisfies the Lane-G finite-corner criterion, but\n49-the two results remain logically independent.\n50-\n--\n55-| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n56-|---|---|---|\n57-| P47 | `CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean` | Define center, central projections, finite projections, corners, central support, and fullness for the concrete von Neumann-algebra model. Prove only algebraic order/corner lemmas; no direct integral. |\n58-| P48 | `GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean` | Formalize the general-lattice exhaustion, local code projections, monotonicity, and the strong-limit projection `q`. If the stabilizer definitions do not imply a required limit fact, expose it as an auxiliary hypothesis. |\n59:| P49 | `FiniteCornerTrace.lean` | Derive finite-stage trace cyclicity and pass it to the compressed quasi-local C-star algebra. Keep finite codespace density data explicit. |\n60:| P49A | `StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean` | Develop the strong-operator convergence/closure API needed for concrete operator algebras; prove commutants and hence concrete von Neumann algebras are strongly closed. This is a proved infrastructure theorem, not an interface. |\n61:| P49B | `VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean` | Prove the analytic double-commutant theorem for a unital complex star subalgebra of bounded operators: its bicommutant is its strong-operator closure. Develop the required finite amplification/cyclic-subspace machinery locally when Mathlib lacks it. |\n62:| P49C | `KaplanskyDensity.lean` | Prove bounded/unit-ball Kaplansky density for the represented C-star algebra in its bicommutant and derive the compressed-corner approximation used by the manuscript. No supplied density interface is accepted. |\n63:| P50 | `NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean` | Using P49 and P49C, prove traciality of `tau_q` on `q M_Gamma q` by bounded strong approximation, then prove normality and faithfulness from the exact vector-functional and density/commutation hypotheses used in the manuscript. |\n64-| P51 | `FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean` | Prove `q` finite, prove fullness, and derive `0 != z ->` a nonzero finite projection in `z M_Gamma`; define/use the project-local type-III obstruction. |\n65-\n66-### Explicit local-hyperbolic lane\n67-\n--\n80-\n81-| Packet | Lean target | Purpose |\n82-|---|---|---|\n83-| P60 | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Optional globalization of a full finite corner to a faithful normal semifinite weight, if needed beyond no-type-III exclusion. |\n84:| P61 | `HyperbolicImpliesCentralCriterion.lean` | Show the explicit Lane-H model supplies the finite-corner criterion used by Lane G. |\n85-\n86-## Initial parallel wave\n87-\n88-Submit only the four independent foundation packets first: P47, P48, P52,\n--\n101-4. No claim that hyperbolic data imply a factor before the spatial tensor\n102-   factorization and factorhood of both factors are proved.\n103-5. Every manuscript-facing packet identifies an exact `main.tex` locator and\n104-   every extra analytic hypothesis appears as a named field, never an axiom.\n105:6. P49A--P49C are mandatory proved infrastructure. P50 may not replace the\n106-   bicommutant theorem or Kaplansky density by a supplied structure field; an\n107:   incomplete analytic package halts Lane G and triggers review.\n108-\n109----\n110-\n111-# Previous single-lane plan: retained background\n\n--- PACKET ---\n# P50 — faithful normal tracial state on the von Neumann corner\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Source basis:** `main.tex:1336-1455`.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P50`; Lane `G`.\n- **Predecessors:** `P49` and `P49C`, integrated and locally audited before submission.\n- **Gate discharged:** extend `tau_q` to `q M_Gamma q` and prove it is a\n  faithful normal finite tracial state under the exact required hypotheses.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no fullness, no statement about every central\n  summand, no global trace/weight, and no final type-III exclusion.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean`. Define the\ncorner functional induced by P49 in the represented von Neumann corner. Use the\nproved P49C bounded compressed approximants and bounded product convergence to\nprove cyclicity on all of `q M_Gamma q`. Prove positivity and unitality directly;\nprove normality from the vector-functional realization; and prove faithfulness\nfrom the manuscript's dense-vector/commuting-complement argument. The conclusion\nmust be a faithful normal finite **tracial state**, not merely a weight.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nList all representation, support, commutation, cyclicity-of-the-global-vector,\nand dense-vector premises explicitly; do not use a global trace. Bicommutant or\nKaplansky density may not remain as auxiliary assumptions because P49C proves them.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean`; import P49,\nP49C, and the checked C-star/GNS infrastructure as needed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n`lake build AristotleCandidates.NormalFaithfulCornerTrace` succeeds without\nforbidden declarations. Positivity, normalization, traciality, normality, and\nfaithfulness must be proved under the explicit manuscript specialization data;\nthe response must name every remaining non-analytic premise.\n\n--- DECISION ---\n# Two-lane formalization decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle loop follows the two-lane plan in `PLAN.md`.\n\n**Lane G** formalizes the manuscript's general-lattice corner argument:\nthe strong-limit code projection `q`, the faithful normal finite tracial state\non `q M_Gamma q`, finiteness and fullness of `q`, and the conclusion that each\nnonzero central summand has a nonzero finite projection and hence is not type\nIII. This route does not use a direct integral and does not require a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`.\n\n**Lane H** formalizes the explicit short-range/local-hyperbolic model:\ncoherent coordinate maps, an algebraic and C-star `alpha`, the product-state\nidentity, product GNS tensor factorization, and the resulting factor and\ntrace/weight classification.\n\nThe lanes meet only after their own gates are met. In particular, the explicit\ntensor-factor result proves trivial center in the special local-hyperbolic\ncase, whereas the general corner result rules out type-III central summands\nwithout asserting trivial center.\n\nThe first approved parallel Aristotle wave is P47, P48, P52, and P54. No\ndependent packet should be submitted before its prerequisite results are\nintegrated and semantically audited.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-07: the analytic passage from the compressed quasi-local\nC-star algebra to the von Neumann corner is mandatory project infrastructure.\nAfter P48, the loop must prove strong closedness of concrete von Neumann\nalgebras (P49A), the analytic double-commutant theorem (P49B), and Kaplansky\nunit-ball density with its compressed-corner corollary (P49C). P50 depends on\nboth the finite-stage/C-star trace P49 and the proved P49C result. These core\nanalytic theorems may require new local topology machinery, but may not be\nreplaced by axioms or supplied interfaces.\n\n--- HANDOFF/STATUS ---\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md\nreviews/P38-concrete-quasilocal-cstar-model-closeout.md\nreviews/P39-state-preserving-gns-model-closeout.md\nreviews/P40-bicommutant-normal-transport-closeout.md\nreviews/P41-product-factor-classification-boundary-closeout.md\nreviews/P47-center-finite-projection-core-closeout.md\nreviews/P48-general-lattice-projection-tower-closeout.md\nreviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-closeout.md\nreviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-recovery.md\nreviews/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann-closeout.md\nreviews/P49B-von-neumann-bicommutant-theorem-closeout.md\nreviews/P49C-kaplansky-density-closeout.md\nreviews/P52-coherent-local-hyperbolic-coordinates-closeout.md\nreviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md\nreviews/P54-uhf-reference-representation-closeout.md\nreviews/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor-closeout.md\nwork/FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md\nwork/FORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- PROJECT AGENTS ---'; sed -n '1,320p' AGENTS.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- P49 REVIEW ---'; sed -n '1,260p' reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-closeout.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- P49C REVIEW ---'; sed -n '1,300p' reviews/P49C-kaplansky-density-closeout.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- FORMALIZATION AUDIT ---'; sed -n '1,260p' work/FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- SEMANTIC AUDIT ---'; sed -n '1,240p' work/FORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- TASK LOG ---'; tail -120 history/logs/20260807T141506Z-4eae2e12-tasks.log; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- CLI REFERENCE ---'; sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/references/aristotle-cli.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- PROJECT AGENTS ---'; sed -n '1,320p' AGENTS.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- P49 REVIEW ---'; sed -n '1,260p' reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-closeout.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- P49C REVIEW ---'; sed -n '1,300p' reviews/P49C-kaplansky-density-closeout.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- FORMALIZATION AUDIT ---'; sed -n '1,260p' work/FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- SEMANTIC AUDIT ---'; sed -n '1,240p' work/FORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- TASK LOG ---'; tail -120 history/logs/20260807T141506Z-4eae2e12-tasks.log; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- CLI REFERENCE ---'; sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/references/aristotle-cli.md\"","aggregated_output":"--- PROJECT AGENTS ---\n# Manuscript-Only Context Policy\n\n## Source authority\n\nFor manuscript-facing statements, the sole mathematical source is\n`sources/manuscript/main.tex`.\nThe local summary and locator record is `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. Do not modify\nthe manuscript from this project.\n\nEvery claim described as coming from the manuscript must identify an exact\nline range in `main.tex`. Repository history, earlier chat context, and other\nartifacts are not substitute sources.\n\n## Context firewall\n\nDo not introduce, assume, or attribute to the manuscript any gLU,\nrefinement, layer-coherence, or finite-coordinate construction unless it is\npresent in the cited manuscript lines or is explicitly introduced as a new\nauxiliary assumption. A Lean file compiling does not make its unstated\nphysical or operator-algebraic hypotheses part of the manuscript.\n\nClassify each item as one of:\n\n1. **manuscript-derived**: exact source locator and no stronger conclusion;\n2. **auxiliary assumption**: explicitly labelled and used only conditionally;\n3. **Lean infrastructure**: reusable formal mathematics that makes no source\n   claim; or\n4. **legacy exploratory work**: retained for reference but unavailable as\n   support for a manuscript-derived assertion.\n\n`CONTEXT-LEDGER.md` records the current legacy items.\n\n## Current formalization boundary\n\nThe target discussed in the manuscript is the short-range regional-algebra\nstatement at `main.tex:1740-1752`; its proposed proof is at\n`main.tex:1891-2004`. Keep separate the asserted algebraic identification,\nthe product-state/GNS steps, the unformalized operator-algebraic completion and\nspatial tensor-product steps, and the trace conclusion. A tracial state is\nappropriate only for the finite pure-sector case. The infinite pure-sector\ntarget instead calls for a faithful normal semifinite trace/weight when the\nrequired hypotheses and von Neumann infrastructure are supplied.\n\n## Aristotle task packets\n\nEvery new task under `aristotle_tasks/` must begin with exactly one context\ndeclaration:\n\n- `Source basis: main.tex:<line range>` for a manuscript-facing task; or\n- `Infrastructure only:` for reusable Lean material that makes no manuscript\n  claim.\n\nIt must then list every auxiliary assumption, state its exact Lean target, and\nsay whether its conclusion is conditional. A task may not cite a legacy\nartifact as its source basis. Use `aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md` for new\npackets.\n\n## Active two-lane plan execution\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle execution plan is `PLAN.md`, with the approval\nrecord in `work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md`. Before starting any new\npackage in the P47--P61 program, read both files and the closeout/audit record\nfor every declared predecessor.\n\nEvery future packet must include a `Plan alignment` section containing:\n\n1. the exact package identifier and its lane: `G` (general finite-corner and\n   central type-III exclusion), `H` (explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor\n   model), `shared`, or `reconnection`;\n2. the predecessor packages that have already been integrated, or `none` for\n   a foundation package;\n3. the exact gate this package is permitted to discharge; and\n4. downstream claims it is forbidden to make.\n\nThe Aristotle prompt must explicitly instruct the worker to read the active\nplan and respect this section. A package may use only integrated, compiled\npredecessors; a finished remote job is not a dependency until it has passed\nthe local semantic audit. Do not infer a theorem from a later package, and do\nnot submit a dependent packet before its listed prerequisites are integrated.\n\nFor Lane G, the required conclusion is a nonzero finite **projection** in\nevery nonzero central summand; a finite-dimensional subalgebra is not enough.\nFor Lane H, do not call the local algebra a factor until the spatial tensor\nfactorization and factorhood of both factors are proved. Neither lane may\nclaim a global trace/weight unless it constructs or explicitly assumes one.\n\n## Verification and reporting\n\nReport Lean compilation separately from mathematical validation. For each\nmanuscript-facing milestone, state which source clauses are represented, which\nassumptions remain external, and which analytic/von Neumann-algebraic claims\nare not yet formalized in the pinned Mathlib version.\n--- P49 REVIEW ---\n# P49 closeout review — finite-stage trace and compressed quasi-local corner\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: partial; queue must halt.**\n\nThe Aristotle result contains a technically sound-looking, conditional candidate\nmodule, but it is not accepted or integrated.  The packet's required source\ndeclaration is `main.tex:1196-1335`, while the candidate explicitly attributes\nits finite-stage cyclicity and codespace-density identities to the manuscript.\nThose identities occur at `main.tex:1133-1191`: in particular, the vector\nfixing calculation is at lines 1133-1148, the functional is stated at\n1150-1158, and finite-stage cyclicity and `eq:local_traciality` are at\n1161-1191.  Lines 1196-1335 begin only with the bounded strong-limit passage\nand then the C-star and von Neumann extensions.  Thus the packet does not give\nthe exact source locator required for all of its manuscript-derived claims.\n\nChanging the packet or candidate locator would be a scope/policy edit outside\nthis bounded closeout.  The candidate remains only in the response quarantine;\nthe live working tree was not given `AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean`.\n\nThe downloaded raw response record is\n`aristotle_responses/P49-finite-corner-trace.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`17ceca9683eb286ebd136fb5fc2238f97fb077f2d1f73dacff93ff548ebe5473`), extracted\nwithout a build, update, or dependency fetch at\n`aristotle_responses/P49-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49-gizp5x2z_aristotle/`.\nIts candidate module has SHA-256\n`38d4cbb58104d88f9830aa6b73846d6309f497f48b4140f762a2f031343be487`.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions reviewed\n\nThe quarantined module declares, under complex Hilbert-space assumptions, the\nfollowing scoped results:\n\n- `tauVec`, `compressL`, and `cornerTau`, with\n  `cornerTau_star_mul_self`, `cornerTau_nonneg`, `cornerTau_one`, and\n  `compressL_mem_corner`;\n- `trace_density_sandwich_comm`, `stabilizerCodeDensity`,\n  `trace_stabilizerCodeDensity`, `trace_groupAverage_eq`, and\n  `posSemidef_smul_of_isIdempotent`;\n- `FiniteCodespaceSystem`, `CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem`, and the derived\n  `FiniteCodespaceSystem.stageProj_apply_self`,\n  `FiniteCodespaceSystem.stage_cyclic`, and\n  `CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem.trace_density_incl`;\n- `tendsto_tauVec_sandwich`, `cornerTau_cyclic_of_stage`,\n  `CornerTracialOn.closure`,\n  `cornerTracialOn_quasilocalCStarAlgebra`, and the packaged conditional\n  theorem `CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem.finite_corner_trace`.\n\nThe candidate's named auxiliary data are explicit: finite stage star\nrepresentations; hermitian idempotent code projections; densities of the form\n`weight n • codeProj n` with trace one; the vector-state identity; compatible\nstage inclusions; the P48 decreasing-projection-tower premise; and a\nnorm-density inclusion into the closure of finite-stage ranges.  No normality,\nfaithfulness on the von Neumann corner, fullness, finiteness of `q`, global\nweight, or type-III conclusion is declared.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | In the live project's Lean environment, the quarantined module type-checks.  Its conditional finite-stage/corner-C-star statements compile, and the four sampled key declarations depend only on `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. |\n| partial | The Lean result is a conditional finite-stage and norm-closed quasi-local statement, not a proof of a trace on `q M_Gamma q`.  More importantly, its source-backed presentation needs the packet locator expanded to cover `main.tex:1133-1191`; that correction is not made in this closeout. |\n| blocked | Acceptance is blocked by the source-locator mismatch.  P50's separate Kaplansky-density/normality passage remains unaddressed, as required. |\n| failed | No Lean compilation or forbidden-declaration failure was found.  The task fails acceptance solely on the mandatory source-authority/context requirement. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is therefore **not accepted at its stated\nmanuscript-facing scope**, despite the successful conditional Lean check.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P49, Lane G — correct.\n- **Predecessors:** P47 and P48 are locally integrated and audited.  Their live\n  SHA-256 values match the corresponding files in quarantine:\n  `c55831ac16d3dec3d471c25c24159a5c22c79dff1460c586830eadda27da57d8`\n  (P47) and\n  `190af007e460f439360a0e195c6458e23f0aa5146009cb7f6b40ece2ea6b2386`\n  (P48).\n- **Permitted gate:** the candidate addresses only finite-stage cyclicity and\n  its norm-closed compressed quasi-local extension, with explicit finite\n  codespace density data.  This is the P49 gate.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected in the candidate.  The scan found\n  no theorem asserting normality, faithfulness, finiteness/fullness, a global\n  trace/weight, Kaplansky density, a double-commutant theorem, or central\n  type-III exclusion.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake env lean <quarantined FiniteCornerTrace.lean>` — passed, run from the\n  already-built live project; no build, update, or fetch was run in quarantine.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.CenterFiniteProjectionCore AristotleCandidates.GeneralLatticeProjectionTower Formalization` — passed.\n- `lake build` — passed.\n- `#print axioms` for `finite_corner_trace`, `stage_cyclic`,\n  `tendsto_tauVec_sandwich`, and `CornerTracialOn.closure` — only `propext`,\n  `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scans of the candidate and its direct\n  project imports — no executable `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`,\n  `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` declaration.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo Lean-term defect was found in the reviewed route: the strong-limit argument\nuses `p_n Omega = Omega` to reduce the product limit to pointwise convergence,\nand the C-star extension uses continuity on the product closure.  The\nacceptance-blocking defect is provenance, not compilation: the declared source\nrange omits the exact finite-stage clauses the candidate claims to formalize.\nCompilation and axiom inspection cannot repair that source mismatch or prove\nthe later von Neumann-algebraic conclusions.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the ignored raw archive and quarantine extraction, for the\nsupervisor's inspection.  Not integrated: `FiniteCornerTrace.lean`.  Preserved\nunchanged: the pre-existing untracked P49A candidate and its closeout review.\nNo manuscript file was changed, and no commit, push, remote submission,\ndependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed.\n--- P49C REVIEW ---\n# P49C closeout review - Kaplansky density and compressed-corner approximation\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated shared-infrastructure scope; queue may advance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P49C-kaplansky-density.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`6ba52fd4f44f836e02dcf62d4d0cb2c66434d36ee860be54161d2f108a158074`) and\nextracted without a build, update, or dependency fetch at\n`aristotle_responses/P49C-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49c-ocehfr10_aristotle/`.\n\nOnly the packet-authorized module `AristotleCandidates/KaplanskyDensity.lean`\nwas integrated. Its SHA-256 is\n`e57deb88999d442a8882f37fd4b956e7d36df5849b460dea9f5aa1c5bd1ddde4` in both\nquarantine and the live project. The ignored archive and quarantine snapshot\nremain raw response records. No manuscript file was changed.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nFor `H` with `[NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]`\nand `A : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H ->L[ℂ] H)`, the integrated module proves:\n\n- `KaplanskyDensity.ball_mem_strongClosure`: if `A` is norm closed, every\n  `x` in `A''` with `‖x‖ <= 1` belongs to the SOT closure of the unit ball of\n  `A`;\n- `KaplanskyDensity.scaled_ball_mem_strongClosure`: the corresponding\n  norm-bounded scaled statement;\n- `KaplanskyDensity.selfAdjoint_mem_strongClosure` and\n  `KaplanskyDensity.selfAdjoint_ball_mem_strongClosure`: the self-adjoint\n  intermediate forms;\n- `KaplanskyDensity.exists_bounded_net` and\n  `KaplanskyDensity.exists_net_compression`: bounded SOT approximation of\n  `qxq` by `qaq` with `a` in `A`;\n- `KaplanskyDensity.exists_net_compression_product`: product-filter SOT\n  convergence in both multiplication orders.\n\nThe only extra analytic premise is `IsClosed (A : Set (H ->L[ℂ] H))`.\nUnitality is inherited from `StarSubalgebra`; completeness supports the\nfinite-amplification Hilbert-space argument. Projections are explicitly given\nby `star q = q` and `q * q = q`. No density, trace, normality, faithfulness,\nfiniteness, or factor statement is supplied as a field or axiom.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The bounded Kaplansky theorem is derived from the P49B SOT bicommutant theorem, a local convex weak-to-strong closure argument, functional calculus for the self-adjoint unit ball, and a local 2 by 2 amplification. The compressed and product-filter corollaries are proved from the resulting bounded nets and P49A bounded SOT multiplication. |\n| partial | None within the P49C gate. The result is abstract concrete-operator infrastructure; it does not yet identify a project-specific represented C-star algebra or its corner trace. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks the stated P49C gate. P50 still must supply traciality, normality, and faithfulness with its own exact hypotheses. |\n| failed | None. No compilation, placeholder, provenance, scope, or forbidden-downstream-claim failure was found. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met. In particular, the result is genuine\ntopological strong-operator closure and a nontrivial bounded net extracted from\nthat closure, rather than a sequential or unbounded-density substitute. The\njoint result uses `l1 ×ˢ l2` and proves both displayed product orders.\n\n## Manuscript boundary\n\nThe packet declares source basis `main.tex:1269-1315`. Those lines are used\nonly as the locator for the intended compressed-algebra-to-von-Neumann-corner\npassage. This module is shared Lean infrastructure; it does not assert that\nthe manuscript's `tau_q` is tracial, normal, or faithful, that `q` is finite\nor full, that any central summand is non-type-III, that a global trace/weight\nexists, or that a Lane-H algebra is a factor.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P49C, lane `shared` -- correct.\n- **Predecessors:** P49B is integrated and locally audited; its imported P49A\n  and bicommutant support are compiled predecessors. No later package is\n  imported.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged exactly: unit-ball/scaled Kaplansky density,\n  compressed-corner approximation, and jointly indexed bounded product SOT\n  convergence.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The source imports only Mathlib\n  and `AristotleCandidates.VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem`; it contains no P50+\n  import, trace/normality/faithfulness theorem, finiteness/fullness/type-III\n  theorem, global trace/weight theorem, or Lane-H factor theorem.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.KaplanskyDensity` -- passed (one\n  non-blocking style suggestion at line 463).\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore AristotleCandidates.StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann AristotleCandidates.VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem AristotleCandidates.KaplanskyDensity Formalization` -- passed.\n- `lake build` -- passed in the already-built live project.\n- `#print axioms` for `ball_mem_strongClosure`,\n  `scaled_ball_mem_strongClosure`, `exists_net_compression`, and\n  `exists_net_compression_product` -- each reports only `propext`,\n  `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scan -- no executable `sorry`, `admit`,\n  user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or `native_decide`;\n  the sole matches are negative-scope documentation.\n- Quarantine/live byte comparison, SHA-256 comparison, and `git diff --check`\n  -- passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked the load-bearing boundary:\nthe closure is Mathlib's SOT closure, the unit-ball restriction is obtained\nbefore nets are extracted, norm-closedness is explicitly used for the\nresolvent's membership in `A`, the zero scaling case is handled, and the two\ncompressed factors are bounded before invoking joint product convergence.\nThe residual risk is deliberately outside P49C: this generic theorem alone\ndoes not establish the manuscript's concrete representation, corner trace,\nnormality, faithfulness, finiteness, fullness, or type classification.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P49C candidate, this review, and the\nignored raw archive/quarantine snapshot. Preserved unchanged: all pre-existing\nuntracked candidates and reviews. No commit, push, manuscript modification,\ndependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed.\n--- FORMALIZATION AUDIT ---\n# Formalization semantic-audit decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe approved deliverable is a semantic audit/tutorial of the Lean\nformalization, rather than another proof package or a compilation report.\n\nThe audit will provide:\n\n1. a status summary separating proved mathematics, conditional interfaces,\n   supplied data, and unformalized claims;\n2. a dependency map from the manuscript's finite-coordinate argument through\n   the algebraic limit, concrete C-star model, GNS transport, bicommutant\n   transport, and product-factor boundary;\n3. a theorem ledger mapping each important natural-language proof sentence to\n   exact Lean declarations, hypotheses, intermediate lemmas, and semantic\n   verdicts; and\n4. a step-by-step Lean reading sequence with code excerpts and direct build or\n   `#check` commands.\n\nThe audit must keep compilation separate from mathematical validity and must\nidentify exact manuscript locators from `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. In particular,\nit must not call the regional hyperfinite-factor theorem proved merely because\nconditional Lean interfaces compile.\n\nThe first pass will inventory the current modules and completed-package\nreviews. Later passes will inspect the principal declarations and their proof\nchains in dependency order.\n--- SEMANTIC AUDIT ---\n# Formalization semantic audit\n\nStatus: first inventory in progress.\n\nThis document is the approved semantic/tutorial audit described in\n`FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md`. It is not itself a proof and does not\nchange the manuscript theorem status.\n\n## Audit verdict convention\n\n- **proved**: the stated Lean theorem follows from its explicit hypotheses and\n  compiles without placeholders;\n- **conditional**: the Lean implication is proved, but one or more hypotheses\n  are supplied structures or external analytic assumptions;\n- **infrastructure**: reusable Lean mathematics with no manuscript claim;\n- **unformalized**: a manuscript step for which no corresponding theorem is\n  currently present;\n- **not aligned**: the Lean conclusion is stronger, weaker, or materially\n  different from the natural-language sentence.\n\nCompilation, axiom reports, and mathematical alignment will be recorded\nseparately.\n\n## Source clauses\n\nThe manuscript-facing audit uses only the locators recorded in\n`SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`:\n\n- `main.tex:1671-1679`: local symplectic basis and finite-support condition;\n- `main.tex:1740-1752`: regional factor theorem statement;\n- `main.tex:1915-1920`: proposed adapted-basis star-isomorphism;\n- `main.tex:1927-1931`: pure/mixed product density state;\n- `main.tex:1945-1967`: GNS, tensor, and factor claims;\n- `main.tex:1970-2004`: quasi-equivalence and normal-folium claims.\n\n## Initial module inventory\n\nThe detailed theorem ledger and dependency graph are the next sections to be\nfilled after inspecting the principal declarations. The current theorem\ncontract itself still says:\n\n```lean\ndef regionalAlgebraTheoremStatus : String :=\n  \"conditional contract pending analytic model\"\n```\n\nThat status is consistent with the source contract and is not to be upgraded\nwithout discharging the missing finite-coordinate, representation, normality,\nand product-classification premises.\n\n## First-pass verdict\n\nThe current formalization is a sequence of conditional bridges, not yet a\nformal proof of the manuscript's regional factor theorem. The strongest\ncurrently checked route is:\n\n```text\nfinite adapted-coordinate data\n  -> finite StarAlgEquiv at each stage\n  -> coherent algebraic direct-limit StarAlgEquiv alpha\n  -> compatible algebraic state transport\n  -> supplied compatible operator representation\n  -> closed operator-range C*-algebra\n  -> supplied state-preserving C*-extension\n  -> GNS unitary and algebraic bicommutant transport\n  -> conditional product-factor/type classification\n```\n\nThe arrows are not all existence theorems. In particular, the source-specific\nfinite coordinate realization, a faithful representation of the algebraic\nlimit, the regional C*-extension, the analytic normality/WOT statements, and\nthe product-factor classification remain explicit premises or missing\nmathematics.\n\n## Status table for the reviewed overnight packages\n\n| Package | Principal Lean object | Semantic verdict | Main external premise |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P37 | `algebraicLimitOperatorRep` | conditional theorem proved | compatible finite-stage operator representations |\n| P38 | `quasilocalCStarAlgebra` | conditional theorem proved | supplied compatible representation; stage injectivity for faithfulness |\n| P39 | `StatePreservingData`, `gnsUnitary` | conditional theorem proved | C*-completion, alpha extension, state identity and continuity |\n| P40 | `bicommutantStarEquiv`, folium transport | algebraic part proved; analytic part conditional | WOT/double-commutant and normal-functional characterizations |\n| P41 | `ProductGNSFactorization` | partial boundary only | supplied factorization/classification; infinite weight interface is incomplete |\n| P42--P46 | no reviewed candidate currently present | not yet audited | candidate/archive status must be established before use |\n\nAll five reviewed packages compile in the local project. Their closeout\nreviews explicitly separate compilation from mathematical scope. P41 is\naccepted only as partial: its infinite-pure `TracialWeightCore` does not yet\nassert positivity, normality, faithfulness, or semifiniteness.\n\n## Dependency spine and one-to-one theorem anchors\n\n### 1. Finite coordinate map\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Given finite adapted source and target word bases, send each source word to a\n> phase-corrected target word.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_word\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_correctedWord\n```\n\nSemantic status: the construction is proved from the fields of\n`FiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData`, but the actual manuscript-specific finite\ndata are not constructed from `main.tex:1671-1679` or `main.tex:1915-1920`.\n\n### 2. Coherence of finite maps\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The finite coordinate maps commute with the inclusions of stages.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nstarEquiv_connecting_of_pauliBasis\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.stageEquiv_connecting\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved when word, label, phase, and connecting-map\ncompatibility are supplied.\n\n### 3. Algebraic infinite map\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Compatible finite maps descend to a unique star-isomorphism of algebraic\n> direct limits.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha_of\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.existsUnique_alpha\n```\n\nSemantic status: this is a genuine algebraic direct-limit theorem, conditional\non the finite coherent family. It is not yet a C*-completion theorem.\n\n### 4. State transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Pull the target product state back along the algebraic alpha.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nTargetStageStates.targetLimitState\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_eq_targetLimitState_alpha\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_isAlgebraicState\n```\n\nSemantic status: the state-level implication is proved from compatible target\nstage states. The infinite product density operator itself is not constructed\nas a von Neumann-algebraic state in this module.\n\n### 5. Algebraic operator representation\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Compatible finite-stage operator representations define a representation of\n> the quasi-local algebra.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_of\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_stage_congr\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_injective\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved conditionally. Injectivity requires stagewise\ninjectivity; no infinite tensor-product Hilbert space is constructed.\n\n### 6. Concrete C*-model\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Complete the quasi-local algebra in the operator norm.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nOperatorRepresentation.rangeClosure\nOperatorRepresentation.embedding\nOperatorRepresentation.denseRange_embedding\n```\n\nand, for the direct-limit range,\n\n```lean\nquasilocalCStarAlgebra\nquasilocalEmbedding\ndenseRange_quasilocalEmbedding\n```\n\nSemantic status: the closure is genuinely constructed inside bounded\noperators, but only after an isometric operator representation is supplied.\nThis does not prove that the manuscript's algebra has such a representation.\n\n### 7. State-preserving GNS transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> A state-preserving C*-isomorphism induces a canonical GNS unitary.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nStatePreservingData.sourceState_eq_pullback\nStatePreservingData.gnsUnitary\nStatePreservingData.gnsUnitary_intertwines\nStatePreservingData.gnsConjStarAlgEquiv\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved from supplied C*-completions, state positivity/order\ndata, continuity, and an exact state identity. It is not a proof of the\nmanuscript's state identity.\n\n### 8. Bicommutant transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The GNS unitary identifies the represented von Neumann algebras.\n\nLean anchors:\n\n```lean\nStarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated\nStarSubalgebra.le_vonNeumannGenerated\nStarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated_le\n--- TASK LOG ---\nID                                   CREATED              NAME                           STATUS         \n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n9d427b3d-c367-4a33-913f-4dbf6a38aa34 40 mins ago          # Autonomous proof-developm... COMPLETE       \n--- CLI REFERENCE ---\n# Aristotle CLI reference\n\n## Setup\n\n- Install: `uv tool install aristotlelib`\n- Verify: `aristotle --version`\n- Authenticate: set `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` in the shell environment, or use the skill wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\nIf the key is stored near the end of `~/.bashrc`, noninteractive commands may not see it because many `.bashrc` files contain:\n\n```bash\ncase $- in\n    *i*) ;;\n      *) return;;\nesac\n```\n\nIn that case, do not rely on `source ~/.bashrc`. Use the wrapper, which reads a literal `export ARISTOTLE_API_KEY=...` assignment without printing it:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize input.md\n```\n\n## Core commands\n\nSubmit a Lean project for sorry filling or proof search:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh submit \"Fill in all sorries\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\nFormalize a TeX or paper source:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize paper.tex --wait --destination output.tar.gz\n```\n\nList recent jobs:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh list --limit 10\n```\n\nDownload a completed job:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh download <project-id> --destination result.tar.gz\n```\n\nPass the key directly for one command only:\n\n```bash\naristotle submit \"My prompt\" --api-key \"$ARISTOTLE_API_KEY\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\n## Recommended project loop\n\n1. Inspect the Lean project locally.\n2. Run the narrowest local build or test that exercises the target files.\n3. Submit a focused Aristotle prompt against the project directory.\n4. Wait for the run if the expected result is a concrete patch.\n5. Download or inspect the produced artifact.\n6. Rebuild locally and repeat with a tighter prompt if needed.\n\n## Prompt shape\n\nKeep prompts short and file-bound. Good prompts mention:\n\n- the exact project directory\n- the theorem or file to work on\n- whether to fill `sorry`s, formalize a statement, or debug a failing proof\n- what counts as a useful partial result\n\nAvoid vague prompts such as \"improve this project\" unless the scope is intentionally broad.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
